module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.fold_shape_visible_to_no_lens

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data fold_shape_visible_to_no_lens: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "fold_shape_visible_to_no_lens" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "a fold shape that lowers to NEITHER a substrate Loop NOR a surviving surface fold call, so no lens can see it: the site is absent from the analyzer's domain rather than refused inside it, and the accumulator it carries is neither proven, nor refused, nor counted (DESIGN section 5 -- a failure arm must refuse, never widen; here it widens into silence)",
    "SPECIMEN AND INSTRUMENT, 2026-09-12. `fold(xs, init: 0, f: step)` -- a fold-family call whose step is passed BY NAME rather than as an fn literal. Ingested through tokenize / parse_module / normalize, the normalized tree contains no ComputationNode Loop and no surface fold call, and `v2.lens.complexity_accumulator_copy.analyze` `count_fold_sites` returns 0 in both the bound and unbound readings. The instrument is the fixture itself: `named_step_snippet` in `src/v2/test/claim/long/accumulator_copy_fold_analysis_test.dag`, whose two witnesses `named_step_fold_refuses_accumulator_unread` and `report_counters_state_the_domain` are the executing evidence and are rostered red at `gunbc.explicit_witness_admission`.",
    "WHAT MAKES IT THIS CLASS RATHER THAN A MISSING FEATURE: the lens ALREADY CARRIES the honest arm for this exact situation and it is unreachable. `v2.lens.complexity_accumulator_copy.analyze` `fold_family_carrier` mints ^fold_accumulator_unread precisely when the seam refuses to yield a carrier -- the named-step case is named in its own carrier note as a Stage B callee-resolution fact -- but the refusal is never reached, because the traversal never recognises a site to refuse ABOUT. So the corpus contains a written, correct, located refusal that no input can trigger, which reads to every reader as coverage. The tell is a domain counter that reports 0 where the source visibly declares 1, and it is only detectable if the counter is asserted SEPARATELY from the verdict.",
    "WHY IT SURVIVED, and it is a property of the evidence rather than of the defect. Both witnesses live in a module that was DARK: `ingest` passed the sealed NormalizedTree carrier where a Node is wanted (missing `.root`, dead since the BL-1 seal), so all 21 witnesses of that file failed at the type level and none of them ever evaluated its subject. The fail-open and the instrument that would have caught it were disabled by the same unrelated defect, which is why un-darkening a module is a discovery operation and not a formality: 17 of those 21 came back green, and the 4 that came back red were pre-existing -- established on a control worktree carrying only the `.root` repair.",
    "REPAIR RECEIPT AND NARROWED POPULATION, 2026-09-13 (still-bee-353, PR #11314). The ARROW-LAMBDA half of this class is closed at the root. `v2.compiler.fold_lowering` `fold_call_step_fn` searched for ONE step production, ^dag_surface_fn_literal, while `v2.extdeps.languages.dag` declares TWO function-value productions reachable in argument position -- `dag_grammar_arrow_lambda_expr` emits ^dag_surface_arrow_lambda. A step spelled `f: (acc, x) => ...` therefore read as `no step form present` and shared one state with a step passed BY NAME, which is a different fact. It is now a closed `FoldStepForm`, both inline forms projecting onto the same two seam inputs through one shared `fold_call_seam_from_step` into the existing spelling-agnostic `fold_call_seam_loop`. MEASURED, one binary, both directions, fixtures differing only in the lambda spelling (the numbers came from a scratch entry point calling `v2.lens.complexity_accumulator_copy.analyze` `count_fold_sites` and `accumulator_copy_findings` directly over the two snippets; the COMMITTED instrument that re-derives them -- executed under claim_batch and by no lane, see the standing receipt below -- is the committed pair `test/fixture_roots/complexity_accumulator_copy/planted_copy_arrow.dag` and `clean_linear_arrow.dag` read through `corpus_rows_for_paths` in `v2.test.claim.complexity.accumulator_copy_corpus_path_test`, which is where a later reader should look rather than at this sentence): baseline arrow_seen 0, arrow_bound 0, arrow_suspect 0; repaired 1, 1, 1, identical to the fn-form row. THE PREDICTION THAT FAILED IS PART OF THE RECEIPT: the repairing lane predicted from structure that the arrow site would be SEEN-but-unbound, because the traversal recognises a site by callee head alone. It is invisible outright. Recognition is spelling-independent and still the site vanishes, which is the fact the next reader needs.",

    "THE POPULATION THIS ROW NOW CARRIES, after the arrow half closed: the BY-NAME step alone -- `fold(xs, init: 0, f: step)` -- measured at ~18 sites across 14 files, against ~2198 arrow-form sites across ~538 files now covered. The instrument is the `named_seen` reading of `count_fold_sites` over `named_step_snippet`, which is 0 both before and after #11314. THE TRIGGER IS THE CAPABILITY AND NOT A CONSTRUCTION: a by-name fold step's accumulator flow is VISIBLE TO THE COMPLEXITY LENS. Two candidate constructions are open and the row is deliberately not committed to either -- a seam Loop whose body is the step REFERENCE with the carrier edge honestly absent, which would reverse the explicit no-Loop ruling beside `body_lowering_fold` `body_lower_try_fold_loop` and change native emission; or a lens-side read of the referenced step declaration, which `v2.lens.complexity_accumulator_copy.analyze` `fold_family_carrier` already names as a Stage B callee-resolution fact and which may need no lowering change at all. The second is DFS-first by ruling (eager-raven-113, 2026-09-13): a lens is a pure reader and lowering is not changed to suit it.",

    "A SECOND SPECIMEN, AND IT IS THE SAME CLASS FROM THE OTHER END: a lens arm reachable on NO ingest route. `count_fold_sites` carries a SURFACE arm -- a `primary_expr` whose `sequence_left_symbol` is in `fold_family_head` -- beside its LOWERED arm. Measured on the tokenize/parse/normalize route with `tree_contains_surface_fold_call`, that arm is false for ALL THREE spellings: fn-form, arrow-form and by-name alike. No surface fold call survives normalize on this path, so the surface arm has never fired and site visibility depends ENTIRELY on a Loop being produced. That is why the arrow site was invisible rather than merely unbound, and it is a permanently-green check in the DESIGN section 4b sense: it reads to every reader as a second, independent way the lens can see a fold, and there is no input on this route for which it is. Owner: the lens authority in eager-raven-113's lane.",

    "THE SEARCH GRAIN IS THE SECOND HALF OF THIS CLASS, AND IT IS THE WORSE HALF: AN INVISIBLE SITE IS SILENT, THIS ONE ANSWERS. Found by review 65699 on the repair itself, 2026-09-13. `parse_subtree_find_production_captured` is a whole-subtree PRE-ORDER FIRST MATCH rather than a read of the step argument, so `fold(xs, init: 0, f: (acc, x) => fold(x, init: acc, f: fn(a, b) returning a))` classified on the INNER fn literal and built a seam Loop whose body and carrier belong to the inner lambda. The copy planted on the OUTER carrier then goes unseen -- not because the site is invisible, but because the lens was handed the wrong accumulator and answered about it CONFIDENTLY. That is DESIGN section 5 fabricated-plausible-output, and it ranks above the invisibility this row was opened for: a silent subject at least leaves a counter reading 0, while a wrong carrier leaves a clean verdict nobody has reason to doubt. The same search reached inside `fold_node` with an `algebra:` record argument, whose step is a RECORD and not a lambda at all. RIGHT GRAIN, adopted (eager-raven-113 ruling 2026-09-13): read the step form at the argument the CALLEE DECLARES -- fold/f, fold_list/cons, fold_list_right/snoc, fold_node/algebra -- and descend only the CAPTURED-CHILD CHAIN, never across siblings; the direct-argument walk stops at every ^dag_surface_arg without descending into one, so an argument belonging to a nested call inside an argument value is unreachable. Instrument: `test/fixture_roots/complexity_accumulator_copy/planted_copy_nested_arrow.dag`, whose outer carrier is `acc` and whose inner is `a`, measured 0 on main AND 0 on the first cut, 1 once the reading is argument-positioned.",

    "THE REPAIR'S FIRST CUT ADDED AN INSTANCE THE UNREPAIRED CORPUS REFUSED, and that is recorded here rather than left in the PR because it is the distinguishing fact of this class: a reading that WIDENS its search to cover a missed shape acquires the neighbouring shapes too. The arrow arm was tried only when no fn literal existed ANYWHERE in the fold-call subtree, so `fold(xs, init: g(y => y), f: step)` -- a by-name step whose init argument happens to carry a lambda -- would have minted a carrier from the WRONG argument's lambda, where main honestly produced FoldCallStepFormUnresolved. The lane found this while verifying the review rather than being told it; the reviewer had framed the ordering as inherited risk. The general form: when the fix for an invisible shape is a broader search, the search must be RE-POSITIONED rather than widened, or the repair converts silence into a confident wrong answer.",

    "THE BARE SINGLE-BINDER ARROW FORM IS A REFUSAL BY CONSTRUCTION, NOT AN OMISSION. `dag_grammar_arrow_lambda_expr` admits `acc => e` as well as `(acc, x) => e`, and the repair gives the one-binder form NO carrier deliberately: a fold step takes (accumulator, item), the grammar admits the single-binder form for ordinary one-argument lambdas, and reading its sole binder as an accumulator would fabricate a carrier the source never declared. The reading refuses (Absent) rather than falling through to a DFS for the first plausible ident, which is the decline-without-cause this class exists to name.",

    "THE RUNG, stated with its ceiling because a fold the lens cannot see is BELOW the floor rather than low on it: found at below-the-floor, since the complexity lens is a required root gate at the compile door and a subject invisible to it is admitted in silence regardless of how the gate is enrolled. The ceiling is STRUCTURALLY GUARANTEED, and it is reachable: fold-family lowering is a closed, decidable set of declared shapes, so a lowering total over that set makes the invisible site unwritable rather than merely detected. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, named as a capability: every fold-family call the source declares lowers to a shape the lens's traversal enumerates -- suspected home `v2.compiler.fold_lowering` or `v2.compiler.body_lowering_fold` rather than the lens, which is why the repair is dispatched as its own item and was deliberately NOT attempted inside the port-reading fix that found it. A diagnostic variant, a roster row, or a lowering that merely reports the shape retires nothing unless the site becomes visible to the traversal.",

    "SECOND SHAPE IN THIS CLASS, AND IT IS NOT THE RARE ONE. 2026-09-13, found by probing the feed BEFORE building a consumer on it rather than after. A fold whose step is an ARROW LAMBDA -- `fold(xs, init: 0, f: (acc, x) => acc + x)` -- is invisible to the same traversal, and this is a DIFFERENT shape from the by-name step already recorded above: both pass a step LITERAL, and only the `fn(acc, x) { ... }` spelling is counted. The discriminating control is a two-file A/B identical in every character except the lambda form, run through `v2.lens.complexity_accumulator_copy.analyze` `count_fold_sites` over `ingest_tree`: the `fn` spelling answers 1 in both the bound and unbound readings and the arrow spelling answers 0 in both. The same instrument answers 0 for `gunbc.bare_name_fork_lens`, a real module whose body is built from folds, and answers 1 for the lens' own fixture `test/fixture_roots/complexity_accumulator_copy/clean_linear.dag`, which is written in the `fn` spelling -- so the fixtures that establish the lens are drawn from the half of the corpus it can see.",

    "WHY THIS ONE MATTERS MORE THAN ITS SIBLING, and the reason is population rather than severity. The by-name step is a spelling the corpus uses occasionally; the arrow step is ORDINARY STYLE in `dag/`, and measured against the visible spelling it is not merely comparable but MORE COMMON -- it appears more times and in more files than the `fn` form the traversal can see. So the invisible half is the larger half, and a reader who assumes the recorded blind spot is a corner case has the population backwards. Re-derive rather than trust this sentence, because a live-tree count rots: count the arrow-form step occurrences under dag with a grep for the literal text `f: (` followed by a parameter list and the fat arrow, against a grep for `f: fn(`, and compare the two. The consequence is that the row above understates its own blast radius: the lens is described in its own module as a required root gate at the compile door, and a large fraction of the corpus' fold sites are admitted in silence -- not because the gate declined them, but because its traversal never recognised a site to decide about.",

    "WHAT THIS COST AND WHAT IT SAVED, recorded because the ORDER of the two operations is the transferable part. The class was found while attempting a lens for the loop-invariant nullary call -- a nullary call resolved inside a fold whose value the fold does not vary -- which was dispatched as item 3 of the gunbc#11181 meta-review. The immediately preceding attempt in that same item, `authored_fixtures_prove_the_core_while_the_host_feed_is_empty`, built a core, witnessed it with nine passing arms and only then discovered its feed was empty. This time the feed was probed FIRST and the consumer was never written, so the cost was two probe runs rather than a lens, a witness file and an instrument. The lens for the loop-invariant call is therefore NOT attempted and NOT declared under a widened coverage bound: a bound invented around a blind spot discovered mid-build is rung inflation rather than a ceiling, and this shape is now rostered here instead.",

    "DFS RECEIPT ON THE BY-NAME HALF, 2026-09-13 (deep-newt-301), answering the ordered question -- is a lens-side read of the referenced step declaration available at lens time -- in two halves, because it has two. THE DECLARATION HALF IS AVAILABLE: for `fn step(acc: Int, x: Int) { .. }` in the same module the normalized root carries `step` as a named Conj member whose target is the lowered Arrow, its first positional child the Conj domain with `acc` as the first named binding (`v2.std.node_query` `arrow_domain_named_param_bindings` reads exactly this) and its body on ^arrow_body_edge. Nothing new is needed to resolve a name to its declaration inside one root. THE SITE HALF IS NOT: `fold(xs, init: 0, f: step)` as the sole body statement lowers to `Transform [ Atom dag_token_lbrace, Atom dag_token_int_literal, Atom step ]` -- the callee and `xs` are dropped and the brace token stands as the operator -- and a non-fold `g(xs, init: 0, f: step)` lowers to the identical tree. That is `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` `call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering` (its own receipt records `{ g(x: 1) }` -> `Transform [ Atom dag_token_lbrace ]`), reached here from the consumer side. There is no fold head for a lens to key on and no argument position for it to read a step name from; recognising the site by the residue of the erasure would be the workaround DESIGN section 5 names as the line-stop signal. So candidate (B) is blocked on that class's trigger and on nothing else, candidate (A) stays fierce-lark-661's ruling, and this lane built neither. The executing witness for the capability, rostered RED at `gunbc.explicit_witness_admission`, is `declared_named_step_fold_copy_is_caught` in `src/v2/test/claim/long/accumulator_copy_fold_analysis_test.dag`: a declared step carrying a planted copy must mint a suspect, which subsumes the weaker unread assertion.",

    "THE CLASS IS WIDER THAN EITHER SPELLING HALF, AND THE ARROW-HALF COVERAGE CLAIM IS BOUNDED BY POSITION, measured 2026-09-13 on the same route with the same planted fold / list_append copy moved between body positions and nothing else changed. As the sole expression of a brace body: seam Loop, counted, suspect minted (`quadratic_fold_has_suspect`). After one `let`: the Bind's body is a bare sequence spine with `fold` as its leftmost atom and every right projection an empty Conj -- fn literal and arguments gone -- count_fold_sites 0, no finding. In a `match` arm and in an `if` branch: count_fold_sites 0, no finding. The FN-LITERAL spelling, which gate_red_quadratic_rejects proves the gate refuses, is admitted in silence at every one of those positions, so the `~2198 arrow-form sites now covered` figure above holds only for sites in the sole-body position. A single-line floor over dag/ and src/v2 (fold-family call lines whose preceding non-blank line is an fn header ending in `{` -- re-derive before quoting) puts roughly two of every five fold-family call lines in that position and the rest outside it. NESTED folds are the exception and the control: a fold inside a sole-body fold's step keeps its surface form inside the retained Loop body and IS counted and classified -- `nested_fold_inside_a_sole_body_fold_is_visible`, green, folds_seen 2 -- which refutes the second-specimen receipt above: the surface arm of count_fold_sites is reachable on this route, inside retained Loop bodies, and is not permanently green. The enrolled evidence is `let_prefixed_fold_copy_is_caught` and `match_arm_fold_copy_is_caught`, rostered RED with dissolution on the erasure class's trigger. NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, restated with the dependency the DFS found: this class cannot climb ahead of `call_expression_erased_at_v2_body_lowering`; once every fold-family call reaches the normalized tree with callee and arguments intact, the lens's existing surface and lowered arms see the site at every position, and the by-name residue reduces to the declaration read already available.",

    "WHERE THE POSITIVE EVIDENCE FOR THIS CLASS EXECUTES, stated at its actual level so the word `enrolled` is not read one rung high (review 65787 on gunbc#11315, 2026-09-14). The DISCRIMINATING REDS are enrolled: `let_prefixed_fold_copy_is_caught`, `match_arm_fold_copy_is_caught`, `declared_named_step_fold_copy_is_caught` are `test fn`s rostered known-red at `gunbc.explicit_witness_admission`, held by the required floor's changed-witness arm (known_red_held on run 34786156711). The POSITIVE CONTROLS are not: `a_planted_copied_accumulator_spelled_with_an_arrow_lambda_is_caught` and siblings in `v2.test.claim.complexity.accumulator_copy_corpus_path_test`, and `nested_fold_inside_a_sole_body_fold_is_visible`, `a_lambda_in_a_non_step_argument_mints_no_carrier`, `an_inline_step_beside_a_decoy_lambda_is_still_caught` in `v2.test.long.accumulator_copy_fold_analysis`, are plain `fn`s executed under claim_batch as local diligence and planned by no lane. That standing was not chosen; every route was tried or read and each refuses. As `test fn`: the long-home arm ran `nested_fold_inside_a_sole_body_fold_is_visible` for its verdict and it PASSED (standing planned-and-passed-with-cost-debt-observed, 1732ms CPU), and the enrolment-margin gate then refused the same identity as newly enrolled over the 302ms p90 envelope -- `v2.workflow.floor_enrolment_margin`, operator ruling 2026-09-11, `RELOCATING THE FILE DOES NOT DISCHARGE IT`. As a `FalsifierSubstrateLongLane` admission with `ExpectWitnessHolds`: that cadence is `DeclaredCadenceUnrealized` since falsifier.yml was deleted at gunbc#8283 (`std.witness_admission`). The local-repo-wet lane rosters host-effect witnesses only, and the ingest-gate overlay is a hand-listed closure gate. So the class this evidence sits in is `gunbc.recurring_failure_mode` `required_lens_red_control_never_executes_from_its_home`, and the rung the gate claims stays Mitigatable at `gunbc.v2_compile_obligation_census` `accumulator_copy_obligation` -- the reds above are what the restoration would flip, and the greens are a DECLARED DROP, `gunbc.rung_drop` `accumulator_copy_positive_controls_off_every_lane` (previous MechanicallyPreventable, temporary Mitigatable, lost as a passenger of the falsifier long-lane executor), whose restoration trigger is an executing lane with a declared ceiling for an ingest-reaching witness -- the front end paid once per run per `long_module_changed_witness_cpu_observed_only`, or the re-added substrate-long executor gunbc#8283 reserved.",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
